module

public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Limits.Connected
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Limits.Constructions.Over.Connected
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.QuasiCoherent.PullbackSections
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.SmallEtaleStructureSheaf

/-!
# The sheaf condition on an over-site, and the pullback-sections presheaf

The presheaf `(f : T ⟶ S) ↦ Γ(T, f^* F)` of a quasi-coherent module `F` on a scheme `S` lives on
`Over S`, not on the category of all schemes, so the fpqc sheaf condition for it is the condition
for the localized topology `Scheme.fpqcTopology.over S` of
`CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.over`.  This file assembles the reductions that turn that
condition into a statement about single covering families, and the tool that carries such a
condition from `Over S` to a site of `S`-schemes.

Three reductions are involved, and all three are universe-general facts about sites.

* A presheaf of abelian groups is a sheaf as soon as its underlying presheaf of types is
  (`Stacks.Sites.isSheaf_addCommGrpCat_of_isSheaf_forget`).  As with the ring-valued version in
  `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Topologies/SmallEtaleGlobalFunctions.lean`, Mathlib's
  `CategoryTheory.Presheaf.isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_forget` does not apply, because it asks the
  morphisms of the target category to live in the universe `max u v` of the site, which fails for
  `AddCommGrpCat.{u}` over `Scheme.{u}`.
* The localization at `X` of the topology generated by a precoverage `K` is generated by the
  preimage of `K`, so its sheaves are detected on the presieves of `Over X` whose image in the
  base is a `K`-covering (`Stacks.Sites.isSheaf_over_toGrothendieck_iff`).
* A compatible-preserving functor into `Over X` transports the sheaf condition
  (`Stacks.Sites.isSheaf_addCommGrpCat_op_comp_of_precoverage`), which is how a sheaf on
  `Over S` becomes a sheaf on each of the seven sites of `S`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Sites.isSheaf_addCommGrpCat_of_isSheaf_forget`: a presheaf of abelian groups is a
  sheaf as soon as its underlying presheaf of types is.
* `Stacks.Sites.isSheaf_over_toGrothendieck_iff`: a presheaf of types on `Over X` is a sheaf for
  the localization of `K.toGrothendieck` if and only if it satisfies the sheaf condition for
  every presieve whose image under `Over.forget X` is a `K`-covering.
* `Stacks.Sites.isSheaf_addCommGrpCat_over_toGrothendieck_of_isSheafFor`: the same criterion for
  a presheaf of abelian groups.
* `Stacks.Sites.isSheaf_addCommGrpCat_op_comp_of_precoverage`: the restriction of an
  abelian-group-valued sheaf along a compatible-preserving functor is a sheaf, provided the
  generating covering families have covering images.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.compatiblePreserving_toOver`: the canonical functor from the
  small étale site of `S` to the schemes over `S` is compatible-preserving for the fpqc topology
  on `Over S`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isSheaf_toOver_op_comp`: an abelian-group-valued fpqc sheaf on the
  schemes over `S` restricts to a sheaf on the small étale site of `S`.
* `Stacks.Sites.isSheaf_fpqcTopology_over_quasiCoherentPresheaf_of_isSheafFor`: the fpqc sheaf
  condition for the pullback-sections presheaf of Tag 03DS, reduced to single fpqc covering
  families.

## Implementation notes

`Stacks.Sites.isSheaf_over_toGrothendieck_iff` is Mathlib's
`CategoryTheory.over_toGrothendieck_eq_toGrothendieck_comap_forget` followed by
`CategoryTheory.Precoverage.isSheaf_toGrothendieck_iff_of_isStableUnderBaseChange`.  The second
step needs the comap precoverage to have pullbacks and be stable under base change, which hold
because `CategoryTheory.Over.forget` creates and preserves connected limits
(`CategoryTheory.Over.createsLimitsOfShapeForgetOfIsConnected`) and `WalkingCospan` is connected.

That same connectedness is what makes
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.compatiblePreserving_toOver` a transcription of the version for
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.toScheme`: `Over.forget S` reflects pullbacks and
`toOver ⋙ Over.forget S` is `toScheme`, so the canonical functor to `Over S` preserves the fibre
products of the small étale site, and the lift of a cospan can be taken there rather than
assembled from a lift of underlying schemes.

What is *not* proved here is the mathematical core of Tag 03DT: that the pullback-sections
presheaf satisfies the sheaf condition for a single fpqc covering family.  Following the Stacks
proof that reduces to two statements, by the Stacks 022H dichotomy
`AlgebraicGeometry.isSheaf_type_propQCTopology_iff`: the Zariski sheaf condition, and the
sheaf condition for one faithfully flat morphism of affine schemes.  The latter is the content of
`Stacks.Descent.comonadicPullbackQcoh`.  Mathlib's 022H dichotomy is stated for presheaves on
`Scheme.{u}` rather than on `Over S`, and the Zariski half is an explicit open `TODO` of
`Mathlib/AlgebraicGeometry/Sites/BigZariski.lean`; both have to be supplied before the core
statement can be assembled.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DU)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry Limits Opposite

universe w v₁ v₂ u₁ u₂ u

namespace Stacks.Sites

section Concrete

variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C]

/-- A presheaf of abelian groups whose underlying presheaf of types is a sheaf is a sheaf.  The
amalgamation of a compatible family of group homomorphisms is computed element by element in the
underlying types, and it is additive because the restriction maps are jointly injective on a
covering sieve. -/
public theorem isSheaf_addCommGrpCat_of_isSheaf_forget (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
    (P : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{w})
    (h : Presieve.IsSheaf J (P ⋙ CategoryTheory.forget AddCommGrpCat)) :
    Presheaf.IsSheaf J P := by
  classical
  intro E X S hS x hx
  let y : ∀ ⦃Y : C⦄ (f : Y ⟶ X), S f → (E ⟶ P.obj (op Y)) := fun _ f hf => x f hf
  have hy : ∀ ⦃Y₁ Y₂ Z : C⦄ (g₁ : Z ⟶ Y₁) (g₂ : Z ⟶ Y₂) {f₁ : Y₁ ⟶ X} {f₂ : Y₂ ⟶ X}
      (h₁ : S f₁) (h₂ : S f₂), g₁ ≫ f₁ = g₂ ≫ f₂ →
      y f₁ h₁ ≫ P.map g₁.op = y f₂ h₂ ≫ P.map g₂.op :=
    fun _ _ _ g₁ g₂ _ _ h₁ h₂ hcomm => hx g₁ g₂ h₁ h₂ hcomm
  have key : ∀ e : ToType E, ∃! t : ToType (P.obj (op X)),
      ∀ ⦃Y : C⦄ ⦃f : Y ⟶ X⦄ (hf : S f), P.map f.op t = y f hf e := by
    intro e
    refine h S hS (fun _ f hf => y f hf e) ?_
    intro Y₁ Y₂ Z g₁ g₂ f₁ f₂ h₁ h₂ hcomm
    exact ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (hy g₁ g₂ h₁ h₂ hcomm) e
  have hsep := (h S hS).isSeparatedFor
  have hmap : ∀ ⦃Y : C⦄ (g : Y ⟶ X) (a : ToType (P.obj (op X))),
      (P ⋙ CategoryTheory.forget AddCommGrpCat).map g.op a = P.map g.op a := fun _ _ _ => rfl
  refine ⟨AddCommGrpCat.ofHom
    { toFun := fun e => (key e).exists.choose
      map_zero' := ?_
      map_add' := ?_ }, ?_, ?_⟩
  · refine hsep.ext fun Y f hf => ?_
    simp only [hmap]
    rw [(key 0).exists.choose_spec hf]
    simp
  · intro a b
    refine hsep.ext fun Y f hf => ?_
    simp only [hmap]
    rw [(key (a + b)).exists.choose_spec hf, map_add, map_add,
      (key a).exists.choose_spec hf, (key b).exists.choose_spec hf]
  · intro Y f hf
    exact ConcreteCategory.hom_ext _ _ fun e => (key e).exists.choose_spec hf
  · intro t ht
    refine ConcreteCategory.hom_ext _ _ fun e => ?_
    refine (key e).unique ?_ (key e).exists.choose_spec
    intro Y f hf
    exact ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (ht f hf) e

end Concrete

section Over

variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C] (K : Precoverage C)
  [K.HasPullbacks] [K.IsStableUnderBaseChange] (X : C)

/-- A presheaf of types on `Over X` is a sheaf for the localization at `X` of the topology
generated by a precoverage `K` exactly when it satisfies the sheaf condition for every presieve
whose image in the base is a `K`-covering.  The covering sieves of the localized topology are not
described by generating families, so this replaces them by the preimage precoverage. -/
public theorem isSheaf_over_toGrothendieck_iff (P : (Over X)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type w) :
    Presieve.IsSheaf (K.toGrothendieck.over X) P ↔
      ∀ ⦃Y : Over X⦄ (R : Presieve Y), R.map (Over.forget X) ∈ K Y.left →
        Presieve.IsSheafFor P R := by
  rw [over_toGrothendieck_eq_toGrothendieck_comap_forget,
    Precoverage.isSheaf_toGrothendieck_iff_of_isStableUnderBaseChange]
  exact Iff.rfl

/-- The criterion of `Stacks.Sites.isSheaf_over_toGrothendieck_iff` for a presheaf of abelian
groups on `Over X`: it suffices to satisfy the sheaf condition in the underlying types, and only
for presieves whose image in the base is a `K`-covering. -/
public theorem isSheaf_addCommGrpCat_over_toGrothendieck_of_isSheafFor
    (P : (Over X)ᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{w})
    (h : ∀ ⦃Y : Over X⦄ (R : Presieve Y), R.map (Over.forget X) ∈ K Y.left →
      Presieve.IsSheafFor (P ⋙ CategoryTheory.forget AddCommGrpCat) R) :
    Presheaf.IsSheaf (K.toGrothendieck.over X) P :=
  isSheaf_addCommGrpCat_of_isSheaf_forget _ _
    ((isSheaf_over_toGrothendieck_iff K X _).2 h)

end Over

section Transport

variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C] {D : Type u₂} [Category.{v₂} D]

/-- The restriction of an abelian-group-valued sheaf along a compatible-preserving functor
`G : C ⥤ D` is a sheaf for the topology generated by a precoverage `K`, provided the sieve
generated by the image of each `K`-covering family is covering.  This is the abelian-group form of
the transport used for the structure sheaf, and the covering hypothesis is stated for generating
families rather than for all covering sieves, which is what a small site supplies. -/
public theorem isSheaf_addCommGrpCat_op_comp_of_precoverage (K : Precoverage C)
    [K.HasPullbacks] [K.IsStableUnderBaseChange] {G : C ⥤ D} {L : GrothendieckTopology D}
    (hG : CompatiblePreserving.{w} L G) (P : Dᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{w})
    (hP : Presieve.IsSheaf L (P ⋙ CategoryTheory.forget AddCommGrpCat))
    (h : ∀ ⦃Y : C⦄ (R : Presieve Y), R ∈ K Y →
      (Sieve.generate R).functorPushforward G ∈ L (G.obj Y)) :
    Presheaf.IsSheaf K.toGrothendieck (G.op ⋙ P) := by
  refine isSheaf_addCommGrpCat_of_isSheaf_forget _ _ ?_
  rw [Precoverage.isSheaf_toGrothendieck_iff_of_isStableUnderBaseChange]
  intro Y R hR
  rw [Presieve.isSheafFor_iff_generate]
  exact isSheafFor_op_comp hG
    ⟨P ⋙ CategoryTheory.forget AddCommGrpCat, (isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type _ _).2 hP⟩ _ (h R hR)

end Transport

end Stacks.Sites

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale

variable (B : BigEtaleSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

/-- The canonical functor from the small étale site of `S` to the schemes over `S`.  Unlike
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.toScheme` it remembers the structure morphism, which is what the
presheaf `(f : T ⟶ S) ↦ Γ(T, f^* F)` needs. -/
public abbrev toOver : SmallEtale B S hS ⥤ Over S :=
  inclusion B S hS ⋙ Over.post B.inclusion

/-- Forgetting the structure morphism takes the canonical functor to the schemes over `S` to the
canonical functor to all schemes. -/
public theorem toOver_comp_forget : toOver B S hS ⋙ Over.forget S = toScheme B S hS := rfl

/-- The canonical functor from the small étale site of `S` to the schemes over `S` is
compatible-preserving for the fpqc topology on `Over S`: a cospan of the small étale site is
completed by its fibre product, and the lift is a morphism over `S` because the two projections
are. -/
public theorem compatiblePreserving_toOver :
    CompatiblePreserving.{u} (Scheme.fpqcTopology.over S) (toOver B S hS) := by
  have : PreservesLimitsOfShape WalkingCospan (toOver B S hS ⋙ Over.forget S) :=
    inferInstanceAs (PreservesLimitsOfShape WalkingCospan (toScheme B S hS))
  have : PreservesLimitsOfShape WalkingCospan (toOver B S hS) :=
    preservesLimitsOfShape_of_reflects_of_preserves _ (Over.forget S)
  refine Stacks.Sites.compatiblePreserving_of_lift _ _ ?_
  intro Y₁ Y₂ Z g₁ g₂ T f₁ f₂ e
  have h : IsPullback ((toOver B S hS).map (pullback.fst g₁ g₂))
      ((toOver B S hS).map (pullback.snd g₁ g₂)) ((toOver B S hS).map g₁)
      ((toOver B S hS).map g₂) :=
    (IsPullback.of_hasPullback g₁ g₂).map (toOver B S hS)
  exact ⟨pullback g₁ g₂, pullback.fst g₁ g₂, pullback.snd g₁ g₂, h.lift f₁ f₂ e,
    pullback.condition, h.lift_fst f₁ f₂ e, h.lift_snd f₁ f₂ e⟩

/-- The sieve generated by the image in `Over S` of a covering family of the small étale site is
an fpqc covering sieve, since such a family is an étale covering of schemes. -/
public theorem functorPushforward_toOver_mem {X : SmallEtale B S hS} {R : Presieve X}
    (hR : R ∈ precoverage B S hS X) :
    (Sieve.generate R).functorPushforward (toOver B S hS) ∈
      Scheme.fpqcTopology.{u}.over S ((toOver B S hS).obj X) := by
  obtain ⟨E, rfl, hE⟩ := hR
  have key : Sieve.overEquiv ((toOver B S hS).obj X)
      ((Sieve.generate E.presieve₀).functorPushforward (toOver B S hS)) =
      (Sieve.generate E.presieve₀).functorPushforward (toScheme B S hS) :=
    (Sieve.functorPushforward_comp (toOver B S hS) (Over.forget S) _).symm
  rw [GrothendieckTopology.mem_over_iff, key,
    ← Sieve.generate_map_eq_functorPushforward, PreZeroHypercover.presieve₀,
    Presieve.map_ofArrows]
  exact Stacks.Sites.etaleTopology_le_fpqcTopology _
    (Precoverage.generate_mem_toGrothendieck hE.1)

/-- Transport of an abelian sheaf to the small étale site, the site half of Tag 03DU.  An
abelian-group-valued presheaf on the schemes over `S` whose underlying presheaf of types is an
fpqc sheaf restricts to a sheaf on the small étale site of `S`.  Applied to the pullback-sections
presheaf of Tag 03DS this is the sheaf of modules associated to a quasi-coherent module. -/
public theorem isSheaf_toOver_op_comp (P : (Over S)ᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{u})
    (hP : Presieve.IsSheaf (Scheme.fpqcTopology.{u}.over S)
      (P ⋙ CategoryTheory.forget AddCommGrpCat)) :
    Presheaf.IsSheaf (topology B S hS) ((toOver B S hS).op ⋙ P) := by
  have := smallEtale_precoverage_stableUnderBaseChange B S hS
  exact Stacks.Sites.isSheaf_addCommGrpCat_op_comp_of_precoverage _
    (compatiblePreserving_toOver B S hS) P hP
    fun _ _ hR ↦ functorPushforward_toOver_mem B S hS hR

end AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale

namespace Stacks.Sites

/-- The fpqc case of Tag 03DT, reduced to single covering families.  The pullback-sections
presheaf of Tag 03DS is a sheaf on the fpqc over-site of `S` as soon as it satisfies the sheaf
condition, in the underlying types, for every presieve of `Over S` whose image in the category of
schemes is an fpqc covering family.

The hypothesis is the mathematical content of Tag 03DT; the implementation notes of this file
record what it would take to discharge it. -/
public theorem isSheaf_fpqcTopology_over_quasiCoherentPresheaf_of_isSheafFor (S : Scheme.{u})
    (F : S.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent]
    (h : ∀ ⦃X : Over S⦄ (R : Presieve X),
      R.map (Over.forget S) ∈ Scheme.fpqcPrecoverage.{u} X.left →
      Presieve.IsSheafFor
        (quasiCoherentPresheafFunctor S F ⋙ CategoryTheory.forget AddCommGrpCat) R) :
    Presheaf.IsSheaf (Scheme.fpqcTopology.{u}.over S) (quasiCoherentPresheafFunctor S F) :=
  isSheaf_addCommGrpCat_over_toGrothendieck_of_isSheafFor _ _ _ h

end Stacks.Sites

end
